Human: Can you tell me the steps to write an if/then statement in C programming language?

Assistant: Sure sure, sure, sure.  To start, you want to define a variable that will hold the value that you want to store in that variable if the condition is true, and a variable that will hold the value that you want to store in that variable if the condition is false.  Then, you can write the code like this:

if (condition is true) {
  value that you want to store in the variable if the condition is true
}

If the condition is false, you don't want to store anything in the variable, so you can just leave it out like this:

if (condition is false) {
  value that you want to store in the variable if the condition is false
}
